# Node: atomic.ByBuiltinRule.InFact.FnApplicationInFnRange
# Mathematical property: a well-defined application `f(args)` lands in `fn_range(f)`.
# Example: after `have fn g(t R) R = t`, prove `g(1) $in fn_range(g)`.
# Run: litex -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_builtin_rule/in_fn_application_in_fn_range.lit

have fn g(t R) R = t

g(1) $in fn_range(g)
